[{:db/id "2273c691-6884-5960-9489-5d738197d00e" :answer/id #uuid "2273c691-6884-5960-9489-5d738197d00e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}1\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "0ffe947f-52e1-584d-be76-77ece40d3f41" :answer/id #uuid "0ffe947f-52e1-584d-be76-77ece40d3f41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}\\int_{0}^{4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}r\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "196f500a-a2af-50e3-9dd1-0ecadbc6d54a" :answer/id #uuid "196f500a-a2af-50e3-9dd1-0ecadbc6d54a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{2}r\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e21ac4be-6b11-5399-80cc-05afed3bd495" :answer/id #uuid "e21ac4be-6b11-5399-80cc-05afed3bd495" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{- 4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}r\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "0afc24b7-4e9b-5fc1-a813-41887ebcebbf" :answer/id #uuid "0afc24b7-4e9b-5fc1-a813-41887ebcebbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}r\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c9146589-ac3d-5d74-94be-b61e9289276d" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9146589-ac3d-5d74-94be-b61e9289276d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["2273c691-6884-5960-9489-5d738197d00e" "0ffe947f-52e1-584d-be76-77ece40d3f41" "196f500a-a2af-50e3-9dd1-0ecadbc6d54a" "e21ac4be-6b11-5399-80cc-05afed3bd495" "0afc24b7-4e9b-5fc1-a813-41887ebcebbf"] :answer-field/correct "0afc24b7-4e9b-5fc1-a813-41887ebcebbf" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "7d4f7134-3d22-5cbc-8e83-54b913ada494" :question/id #uuid "7d4f7134-3d22-5cbc-8e83-54b913ada494" :question/problem "If $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-2)^{2}+y^{2}\\le 4\\},$ then $\\iint_D 1\\,\\mathrm{d}A=$\n\nChoose the polar setup whose bounds describe $D$ with $r\\ge 0$ and whose integrand is the given Cartesian integrand multiplied by the Jacobian $r.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to change the coordinate system from Cartesian coordinates to polar coordinates. To do this, we will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n\\iint_D f(x,y)\\,dA=\\iint_\\Delta f(r\\cos\\theta,r\\sin\\theta)\\,r\\,dr\\,d\\theta.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch our region $D:$\n\n![](images/86/866f3162cd881e997f28cea68fe22fc90b8ef011b6d8beff00ef38d9a69d2eb9.png)\n\nNotice that the region $D$ represents the disk of radius $2$ centered at $(2,0).$\n\nCartesian and polar coordinates are connected by the following equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\cos\\theta \\\\ y=r\\sin\\theta\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the $(x-2)^{2}+y^{2}=4$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+y^{2}&=4\\\\(r\\cos\\theta-2)^2+(r\\sin\\theta)^2&=4\\\\r^2\\cos^2\\theta-4r\\cos\\theta+4+r^2\\sin^2\\theta&=4\\\\r^2(\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta)-4r\\cos\\theta&=0\\\\r^2-4r\\cos\\theta&=0\\\\r(r-4\\cos\\theta)&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire circle, we must have $r=4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}.$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits for $r$ and $\\theta.$ First of all, $r$ can vary from $r=0$ (at the origin) to $r=4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}$ (at the boundary of the region):\n\n![](images/6c/6c841a1dc73b8a68ba8d51bb4d0f8d1ff051f8d1c0bafdfdbfac134ccbc651aa.png)\n\nSecondly, $\\theta$ can vary between $\\theta=- \\frac{\\pi}{2}$ and $\\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{2}.$\n\n![](images/08/083360143d05d210dcbd11ed86c3a5cc0f2510beeecb68a210e9f52632609867.png)\n\nSo, in polar coordinates $(r,\\theta),$ the region can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(r,\\theta)\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)},\\,- \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\le\\theta\\le \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D 1\\,dA&=\\iint_\\Delta (1)\\,r\\,dr\\,d\\theta\\\\&=\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}r\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["c9146589-ac3d-5d74-94be-b61e9289276d"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "ad2bb1be-7c1c-50a0-8af1-048b30c61a71" :answer/id #uuid "ad2bb1be-7c1c-50a0-8af1-048b30c61a71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{- 4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}1\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "3e7adafb-1edd-5777-af5d-4c1cdf3fb5bb" :answer/id #uuid "3e7adafb-1edd-5777-af5d-4c1cdf3fb5bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}\\int_{0}^{- 4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}r\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "298cf0ac-ab43-5882-91a6-e7348499b76f" :answer/id #uuid "298cf0ac-ab43-5882-91a6-e7348499b76f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{2}r\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "15cbb851-3dfc-5f92-8728-a8b8eec6ed2b" :answer/id #uuid "15cbb851-3dfc-5f92-8728-a8b8eec6ed2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}r\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "21ffbbe1-7ca1-5c19-9aef-3f70c88274e7" :answer/id #uuid "21ffbbe1-7ca1-5c19-9aef-3f70c88274e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{- 4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}r\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c09a0523-101d-5678-835e-b363f24d33b3" :answer-field/id #uuid "c09a0523-101d-5678-835e-b363f24d33b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["ad2bb1be-7c1c-50a0-8af1-048b30c61a71" "3e7adafb-1edd-5777-af5d-4c1cdf3fb5bb" "298cf0ac-ab43-5882-91a6-e7348499b76f" "15cbb851-3dfc-5f92-8728-a8b8eec6ed2b" "21ffbbe1-7ca1-5c19-9aef-3f70c88274e7"] :answer-field/correct "21ffbbe1-7ca1-5c19-9aef-3f70c88274e7" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "9021eafc-a91a-5e03-85b9-0baff1b49b29" :question/id #uuid "9021eafc-a91a-5e03-85b9-0baff1b49b29" :question/problem "If $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+2)^{2}+y^{2}\\le 4\\},$ then $\\iint_D 1\\,\\mathrm{d}A=$\n\nChoose the polar setup whose bounds describe $D$ with $r\\ge 0$ and whose integrand is the given Cartesian integrand multiplied by the Jacobian $r.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to change the coordinate system from Cartesian coordinates to polar coordinates. To do this, we will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n\\iint_D f(x,y)\\,dA=\\iint_\\Delta f(r\\cos\\theta,r\\sin\\theta)\\,r\\,dr\\,d\\theta.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch our region $D:$\n\n![](images/3a/3a77e854cc9553675752e3e4e231c8915d390091a4f4fa22cee2eb5ffe279c3e.png)\n\nNotice that the region $D$ represents the disk of radius $2$ centered at $(-2,0).$\n\nCartesian and polar coordinates are connected by the following equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\cos\\theta \\\\ y=r\\sin\\theta\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the $(x+2)^{2}+y^{2}=4$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2)^{2}+y^{2}&=4\\\\(r\\cos\\theta+2)^2+(r\\sin\\theta)^2&=4\\\\r^2\\cos^2\\theta+4r\\cos\\theta+4+r^2\\sin^2\\theta&=4\\\\r^2(\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta)+4r\\cos\\theta&=0\\\\r^2+4r\\cos\\theta&=0\\\\r(r+4\\cos\\theta)&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire circle, we must have $r=- 4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}.$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits for $r$ and $\\theta.$ First of all, $r$ can vary from $r=0$ (at the origin) to $r=- 4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}$ (at the boundary of the region):\n\n![](images/a9/a934a520dfc672601e31dd73fc71a06505f41b6088325a30b49f4d7d99d0f0d7.png)\n\nSecondly, $\\theta$ can vary between $\\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ and $\\theta=\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}.$\n\n![](images/d5/d5b43bd12ba3ca3b3dd69560c728f9c7b16d2d8331702cc3921e8457f53c294f.png)\n\nSo, in polar coordinates $(r,\\theta),$ the region can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(r,\\theta)\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le - 4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)},\\,\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\le\\theta\\le \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D 1\\,dA&=\\iint_\\Delta (1)\\,r\\,dr\\,d\\theta\\\\&=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{- 4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}r\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["c09a0523-101d-5678-835e-b363f24d33b3"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "290abe19-a5e8-5f16-ac8a-3c254b59ca02" :answer/id #uuid "290abe19-a5e8-5f16-ac8a-3c254b59ca02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\pi}\\int_{0}^{4 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}1\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "b5fcfdca-6265-5fab-9691-6ac1a660390c" :answer/id #uuid "b5fcfdca-6265-5fab-9691-6ac1a660390c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}\\int_{0}^{4 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}r\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "22fabb63-36cb-5c3f-98b6-b4f2b8a1b771" :answer/id #uuid "22fabb63-36cb-5c3f-98b6-b4f2b8a1b771" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\pi}\\int_{0}^{2}r\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a87eed07-0b8a-5520-9c6e-109e5f040429" :answer/id #uuid "a87eed07-0b8a-5520-